{"title":"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Summary\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Summary</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3dbce4e72ad7c1746623d1dfc9bbd46cad07cb91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{Z}^+ \\to \\mathbb{Z}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03fae0974b852c6df5091d7f45ca46d26429986a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Z}^+$\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the set of positive integers) such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23dc6c08a472f61de7cc4337c2a8fd614883ee17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n!) = f(n)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39dd48954afea6461cb5f99e7d4d0cfb274cdc52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - n$\" width=\"48\" height=\"8\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f4148177aeebb6883fddcfe5629cc633ac411f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m) - f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> for all distinct positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the first condition we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbf938d1dd3df858869af5ec14d1ed30841c0b3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=f(1!)=f(1)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f611a0ab44aa0a4a0dc319a76bda28266bd45bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=f(2!)=f(2)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc73712d7f1001a98e82f12a2706d1004bae0610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and similarly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/562a91083e33775cdf050ea94f9e84d78a9c071c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />.  By the second condition, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83e525af064ded0b34353ed5b9ba8f90dc91df9a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n\\cdot n!=(n+1)!-n! \\mid f(n+1)!-f(n)! \\qquad \\qquad (1)\\]\" width=\"402\" height=\"18\" />\nfor all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose that for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/8898f48ba4c01f29d31847adf068affbe88b0812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />.  We claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/0/a905102b6b57f88f47a56b4deca10d923e5b36c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/d/95d2e067d1478ce981661242d54d5fa608f60321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\ge n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />. Indeed, from Equation (1) we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/f/e7f467bf30a1fd72e0f5b9bf8e98861e3c10aefc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n+1)!\\equiv 1 \\mod n\\cdot n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />, and this is only possible if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de9d3bdd933f93a6839c75ea8199e1679831a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n+1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />; the claim follows by induction.\n</p><p>We now divide into cases:\n</p><p><b>Case 1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8e38a693765b2a79ffdaa1eb3a65e6ca0155fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=f(2)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97de2bd2007b26ce861949134d8b687eddb368b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> always from the previous claim, which is a solution. \n</p><p><b>Case 2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1eac8a094f7530d220f284b5bb90af0e78587ee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=2, f(2)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97de2bd2007b26ce861949134d8b687eddb368b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39abfe232e2ed5247aa4028089e5f651090e66da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, but this does not satisfy the initial conditions. Indeed, we would have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac9adf9d7391e6dba5107ff6c550550fa7007d4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3-1 \\mid f(3)-f(1)\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />\nand so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd0b9f0b4348d3fe050bef203e0d2ac15151b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\mid -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />, a contradiction.\n</p><p><b>Case 3:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc73712d7f1001a98e82f12a2706d1004bae0610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/e/64eb03e53983d05c3e97b121504a882e16901e22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639d19f96e7aa389ed47ed3164ed7979e1e1c9ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> always by induction. The base cases are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Fix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83ffe7f081bfaaca429cf1f3c1c33abf88744951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />.  By Equation (1) we have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edc2fd3504f5bfbf3a1679c8abf2705c00e0e62b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(k+1)! \\equiv k! \\mod k\\cdot k! .\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />\nThis implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b1180ea5b46d159e3c1a630e778f3d97bc1f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k+1)&lt;2k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> (otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/4/92408bcf5f644e4a45df7e33ee0d3122c9cd1a52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k+1)!\\equiv 0 \\mod k\\cdot k!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />). Also we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ce3e2982091ffb8ebcb8e089efecc3460c8071a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(k+1)-1  \\mid  f(k+1)-f(1)\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"18\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/5458ceb7df5e611b9482c8656ee27fcc565f7951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k+1)\\equiv 1 \\mod k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />. This gives the solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17e36c42c329b4b00381f833903afdaad34e7669.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k+1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efac9633b588d7791574c50323fe37bd4515d0de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k+1)=k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />. The first case is obviously impossible, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b147440414e7796356d975c4c70e0bd34954e993.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k + 1) = k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" />, as desired.  By induction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/e/78e4d0b2e6d053bfe0109e52affa87bcce39d9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  This also satisfies the requirements.\n</p><p><b>Case 4:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a7c0c228010e0eaa1e452e55855ad18c68809e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=f(2)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We claim <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b3fe4ce6145dbfba920142706eed2e29ba60abf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> by a similar induction. Again if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3cba9348532e8339d75f31ea93b7444b108dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />, then by (1) we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7efb255c9b80f595d064afa56505e30390fc000.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(k+1)\\equiv 2 \\mod k\\cdot k!\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" />\nand so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b1180ea5b46d159e3c1a630e778f3d97bc1f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k+1)&lt;2k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />.  Also note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/8/7e8b6970c1c549c187a5331a1805d1a0a86afefe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k+1-1  \\mid  f(k+1)-2\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a09642e03b382122917402cf6b3bedaa3b18b1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k+1-2  \\mid  f(k+1)-2\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/7/63789dd9c6ccc088f47f1602dd9af266b3f89590.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k+1)\\equiv 2 \\mod k(k-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" />. Then the only possible solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/a/f4ab0190790e5485c3f5ef205a0edc13652b9041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(k+1)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />. By induction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/6/2169dd7c117e33c7fd55baad17d6046233e0e276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and this satisfies all requirements.\n</p><p><br />\nIn summary, there are three solutions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43c77d59332f8c80f81066e8196ce3431ea9b5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{f(n)=1, f(n)=2, f(n)=n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"239\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Summary\">Summary</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Summary\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three functions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/4874544e2638f3712dbb70e5ccf37558a5fc0acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b56721c420173cb0be842fac3a097f827ef2dc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x!=x!$\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/5704a6bd9c2f670b45dabc70e2e5cf93dc742161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1!=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/46377b53287d0b7f76190da9e05acbd0fdedd334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2!=2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />, fixed points on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/2950e3accfad26309bf1ecf6947061171fd2797f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x!$\" width=\"14\" height=\"13\" /> function.\n</p><p>No elegant<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ece84ccd8b6babbc8fe4cc51c9f4815ccc5f108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> argument needed; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83e8d764506a6efda13217f253d16146d03fbae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m)-f(n)\\textcolor{red}{\\textbf{ = }}m-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"20\" /> so of course <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/07843d1a57e3c5bb8910817a0dbe57f07d26f30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-n\\mid f(m)-f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fc7643bed309cd7198ca7c2787f248b4788d612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" /> and notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd37cd85dbbf707c808b2982da7c85a34f617a69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c! = c \\implies (c-1)! = 1 \\implies c = 1,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"296\" height=\"20\" />, hence the polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b45226181d75585133e6b537cb9c29cd65dfcc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 1,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> work.\n</p><p>Now, we find all other functions which are nonconstant. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a121da25c1a8bb8e3af01549e741096cc535861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = a_dx^d + \\dots + a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"22\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/619eed35bee9014d8340b1daf8074bc90c3de03b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n!) = a_d (n!)^d + \\dots + a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"22\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/5/425006c3f17a1632b95b7e0c9d539c493f25b0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(f(n))! = (f(n))(f(n)-1)(\\dots)(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"274\" height=\"20\" />. Hence the equality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a1b346767ba494f0ff0c4845e977dc97f1b3de8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n!) = a_d (n!)^d + \\dots + a_0 =  (f(n))(f(n)-1)(\\dots)(1)\\]\" width=\"418\" height=\"20\" />\nholds. The leading coefficients satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/2/60223900145ea68110ca04d5e94429d77bad8378.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_d = a_d^n \\implies a_d = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>However, the degree of the left side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the degree of the right is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7ebe81512ebeaaa8e00a46a6b9b7eda7663a6dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/87966f79c2baac975c33f54e5780478d92136ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = d!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, and that only works if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/083bc41a8797b98d68a874b6b1184b57bee49754.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = (d-1)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/3173fa662c519084af54a3128ce7b3ecb7ee08e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 1,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad2990977902054f4d1da49fba330ce8139e7859.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, it is easy to see the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/4874544e2638f3712dbb70e5ccf37558a5fc0acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> works. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/d/fbd68fc9b0e901c556adb5c363357d3afbf1b4ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/4680fdf57988411955040b96a2447e359f42bad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n!)^2 + b(n!)+ c = (n^2+bn+c)(n^2+bn+c-1)(\\dots)(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"454\" height=\"21\" />. Checking degree however we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36ed6644f87b3ebd2601f15f01db68717840df89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\neq m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/1/ac13426fcb6f49a81f28e4c23ccef7321c0037f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> is the degree of the RHS. Hence, a contradiction.\n</p><p>The only three polynomials are from the family \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/6/d763d8d9cc852d9dc57305e038c92f41fe539ca3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{f(x) = 1, f(x) = 2, f(x) = x} \\quad \\forall \\ x\\]\" width=\"277\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>It easily follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25df2330156e8d513177480557ae8f0680086286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-n \\mid f(m)-f(n) \\qquad \\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><b>Remark:</b>\n</p><p>One can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> is a polynomial here rather than an arbitrary function as \n</p>\n<ul><li>the statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad84c7b7cc40837035c913c907c84a0ee727cb94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n!) = (f(n))!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" /> is nested</li></ul>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has the property for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46ba6ed097cc88ded349bf99eea89817f135f470.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a71cb224223ce9b2b5ae36b56467731b9f6eac30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-n \\mid f(m) - f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>The second condition is true for all polynomials, and the <b>second uniqueness lemma</b>, makes the first condition true. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> was not a polynomial, then it follows that both properties cannot hold simultaneously, particularly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a71cb224223ce9b2b5ae36b56467731b9f6eac30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-n \\mid f(m) - f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" /> as I can construct a non-continuous function that satisfies rule 1 but breaks rule 2 or vice versa.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO\" title=\"2012 USAMO\">2012 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017231112\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.075 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 514/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16730/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.488      1 -total\n 59.65%    8.045      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 37.84%    5.104      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11054:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017231112 and revision id 289710. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}